 "_comment": [
  "Intensity ladder for ABR-HTR option labels. Higher score = more of the thing",
  "the question asks about, NOT more favourable -- favourability is derived by",
  "combining intensity with the question's construct polarity, because 'A lot'",
  "is the best answer to 'did you like it' and the worst answer to 'was it boring'.",
  "",
  "Matching is longest-phrase-first on the normalised label, so 'not at all' wins",
  "over 'at all' and 'did not like it much' wins over 'not'.",
  "",
  "Edit this file, re-run tools/03_scale_map.py, and diff out/scale_map.csv.",
  "Never edit a rank in the output by hand: the output is generated.",
  "Compound phrases matter: 'very uncomfortable' must be listed, because longest-match on 'very' alone scores it as favourable. The rho cross-check in stage 3 catches this class of error, but only after it has already mis-ranked the question -- so add the compound."
 ],
